                <pb facs="0732" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/6:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-24T10:00:00-05:45">May 24, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>61. Department’s 39, May 8, 7 p.m. The Supreme Court of Nicaragua on May 23 named
                    Captain Alfred Wilkinson Johnson, President of the National Board of
                    Elections.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
